'''Samson''' is a [[character]] unlocked by beating two floors in a row without taking any damage.
Samson starts with 3 [[Red Heart container]]s and {{i|Bloody Lust}}.

{{dlc|a+}} Samson will also start with {{t|Child's Heart}} after completing the [[Ultra Hard]] challenge.

== Notes ==
* Due to Samson's starting item, {{i|Bloody Lust}}, he has a playstyle that is similar to {{C|Eve}}. Therefore, health sacrifices such as {{M|Devil Beggar}}s, {{R|Sacrifice Room}}s, and {{M|Blood Donation Machine}}s are recommended.
** As a result, anything that lowers health is not recommended, as that will make self-damage less effective. {{R|Angel Room}}s are more valuable than {{R|Devil Room}}s, if the player comes across any.
* {{dlc|nr}} The first three times Samson is hit, his damage is increased by 0.5. The next three times Samson is hit, his damage is increased by 33%.
* {{dlc|r}} Damage is increased by flat amounts: +0.5 for the first hit and an additional +0.2 for each hit, until +1.5 at the sixth. This means that the maximum total is +6.0.
* Samson's starting trinket, {{t|Child's Heart}}, is one of the more optional unlocks — the trinket itself is not too powerful, not to mention it requiring the completion of the [[Ultra Hard]] challenge.
* When Samson dies in [[co-op]], his ghost baby maintains his level of rage from Bloody Lust, giving it a red tint. This is purely visual.
* Dying as Samson and then respawning as another character (with {{i|Lazarus' Rags}}, {{i|Ankh}}, etc.) will make them inherit Samson's {{i|Bloody Lust}} item.

== Item Interactions ==
* {{i|Birthright}}: {{I|Bloody Lust}} can gain 4 more damage boosts at the same +0.2 intervals, for a new maximum total of +14.0.

=== Favorable items ===
* Any items that increase health so Samson can take more damage before dying.
* Any items that increase Samson's tears stat, such as {{i|Squeezy}}, {{i|Odd Mushroom (Thin)}}, etc.
* Any items that [[Familiar|generate Blue Flies]], like {{i|Rotten Baby}} or {{i|Guppy's Head}}, do so based on Samson's base damage and are good for early game room clearing when Samson's tears are still low.
* Items relying on contact damage, like {{i|The Virus}} or {{i|E. Coli}}, can be beneficial in that damage is desirable with {{i|Bloody Lust}}.
* Health regeneration items like {{i|Yum Heart}}, {{i|Pyromaniac}}, and {{i|Placenta}} allow health regeneration after taking damage, and thus allow for more damage, both stat-wise and health-wise.
* {{I|Old Bandage}} increases Samson's health while also providing a regeneration of sorts, allowing him to take much more damage.
* {{i|Cancer}} and {{i|The Wafer}} minimize damage taken from Sacrifice Rooms and can be incredibly useful to build a lot of damage and pickups, especially in combination with an excess of hearts. The Wafer in particular is incredibly helpful in [[Chapter 4]] and beyond, where all taken damage increases to one full heart per instance.
* {{i|Dead Bird}}, {{i|Best Bud}}, {{i|Smart Fly}}, etc: All of these items will add to Samson's damage increase from getting hurt, although, unlike Bloody Lust, the bonus of these items only last for the duration of a room.
* {{i|Fanny Pack}}'s chance of dropping a heart upon hit can cancel out damage to Samson while also buffing him.
* {{i|Dull Razor}} can safely provide Samson's damage boost without needing to take damage.
* {{i|Gimpy}} increases benefits from taking damage and feasibly adds more survivability from random soul hearts and half-heart drops.
* {{i|Immaculate Conception}} and {{i|Cambion Conception}} will produce familiars as Samson heals or receives damage, respectively.
* {{i|IV Bag}}, {{i|Blood Rights}}, {{i|Razor Blade}}, {{i|Sharp Plug}}, {{i|Kamikaze!}}: Activating their effects also gives Samson a boost in damage since they deal self-damage.
* {{i|Blood Oath}} is extremely useful on Samson, as its damage up effect stacks with {{i|Bloody Lust}}, granting a significant amount of damage up upon the start of a new floor.

=== Unfavorable items ===
* Anything which lowers health, such as {{i|Dead Cat}}, can make purposeful self-damage less reliable as a damage booster. For this reason, taking items from the {{R|Devil Room}} or the {{R|Black Market}}, which cost health for every item thus taken, is not recommended for Samson.

